# libj89

A minimal, strict-C89-clean JSON parser used by the `wid` sibling project.

Subset: object, array, string (escapes, `\uXXXX`, UTF-8), integer,
fractional/exponent number (FLOAT), `true`/`false`/`null`. Strings and object
keys are validated as UTF-8 on input; a single leading UTF-8 BOM is ignored;
duplicate object keys are rejected.

Unicode scalar and UTF-8/UTF-16 facts are delegated to the sibling `libu89`;
`libj89` owns JSON syntax and representation. Every string value and object
key in a `j89_arena` is well-formed UTF-8, whether parsed or built through the
public builder, which validates before allocating. JSON strings are not
normalized or case-folded. Build and test require `libu89` (see `just deps`).

All numbers are IEEE-754 `double`. Integers are exact for |n| <= 2^53; an
integer token beyond that range is rejected (never approximated). This
range/precision limit is permitted by RFC 8259 section 6. A number whose
magnitude exceeds `double` range is rejected (no infinity/NaN).

Constraints:
- ISO C89.
- Green: the sibling `green` toolchain (strict C89∩C23 profile matrix,
  semantic clang-tidy, canonical format) passes for every source. This is
  the conformance gate.
- JSON parsing is intentionally narrow to keep the parser small and
  trivially auditable.

Build and test via `just`.

## Layout

- `src/` — parser, value tree, printer, CLI
- `include/` — public header `j89.h`
- `test/` — unit + e2e tests
- `scripts/` — build helpers (compile-database generation for green)
- `.agent/` — concept, design, stories, scenarios, acceptance

## Recipes

- `just deps` — build the sibling `libu89` dependency
- `just build` — compile the library and `j89` CLI
- `just test` — run unit + e2e tests
- `just check` — unicode-audit + green gate (matrix + tidy + format)
- `just green` — green `check` (matrix + tidy + format; needs `green.yaml`)
- `just unicode-audit` — tripwire: no UTF-8/UTF-16 algorithm in `src/`
- `just lint` — shellcheck + clang-format + source audits

`green.yaml` and the compile databases (generated into `build/` by
`just green-db`) record the gcc and clang compile contexts for the j89
translation units.
